{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_RLuqoezrqnD0c8oRKOGmBpj6","content":"Title: kuranov/intervals-icu-tools\nSite: Github\nDate: 2024-01-01\nURL: https://github.com/kuranov/intervals-icu-tools\nSnippet: ... intervals.icu/oauth/authorize'); authUrl.searchParams.set('client_id ... set('response_type', 'code'); authUrl.searchParams.set('scope', 'ACTIVITY:READ ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: Hosted MCP OAuth: stale DCR client_id is permanently unrecoverable — /v1/oauth/authorize returns 422 {\"message\":\"Unrecognized client_id\"}\nSite: Github\nDate: 2026-08-06\nURL: https://github.com/supabase/mcp/issues/355\nSnippet: To Reproduce |stored `client_id`|result| |-|-| |stored `client_id`|result| |-|-| |`6e1463bb-9600-4640-947d-c1eb4fa2c239`|`303` — still valid| |`07a99c22-a701-4af5-9df7-3f59e4a3d2c8`|`422 {\"message\":\"Unrecognized client_id\"}`| (Client IDs are not secrets; the corresponding `client_secret` s are withheld. Feel free to look up `07a99c22-…` on your side — that record should show whatever happened to it.) So the failing state is not a malformed request from the client. It is a previously-valid, serve\n\n---\n\nTitle: Authorize - OAuth請求授權 - Alibaba Cloud\nSite: Alibaba Cloud\nDate: 2026-07-28\nURL: https://www.alibabacloud.com/help/tc/pds/drive-and-photo-service-dev/developer-reference/api-pds-2022-03-01-authorize\nSnippet: 介面說明 調試 您可以在OpenAPI Explorer中直接運行該介面，免去您計算簽名的困擾。運行成功後，OpenAPI Explorer可以自動產生SDK程式碼範例。 調試 授權資訊 請求文法 ```hljs plaintext GET /v2/oauth/authorize HTTP/1.1 ```\n\n---\n\nTitle: Authorize - OAuth请求授权 - Alibaba Cloud\nSite: Alibaba Cloud\nDate: 2026-07-28\nURL: https://www.alibabacloud.com/help/zh/pds/drive-and-photo-service-dev/developer-reference/api-pds-2022-03-01-authorize\nSnippet: 请求参数 |名称|类型|必填|描述|示例值| |-|-|-|-|-| |domain_id|string|是||| |client_id|string|是|创建 App 时返回的 AppID|47eUHhrzgWBvlLWj| |redirect_uri|string|是|回调地址（创建 App 时填写的回调地址）。请使用 urlencode 对链接进行处理|https%3A%2F%2Fwww.aliyunpds.com%2Fsign%2Fcallback| |scope|array|否|申请的权限列表, 默认为所有权限|| ||string|否|当前仅支持获取 App 的所有权限，可以传 all 或者不传此参数|all| |response_type|string|是|返回类型, 只能填写 code|code| |state|string|否|用户自定义字段\n\n---\n\nTitle: 王逗逗/oauth2-authorize: 手写 OAuth 2.0 授权服务\nSite: Gitee\nDate: 2021-08-05\nURL: https://gitee.com/thousmile/oauth2-authorize\nSnippet: 授权码模式 5.通过上一步获取的 access_token 参数，获取用户信息 ```hljs hljs- GET http://localhost:8098/loginInfo Content-Type: application/json Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}} response: { \"status\": 200, \"message\": \"ok\", \"data\": { \"tokenId\": \"ac44d5f3646f43cda94e72fcb1ddcfe5\", \"grantType\": \"authorization_code\", \"user\": { \"userId\": 609429132107067392, \"avatar\": \"https://images.xaaef.com/b9a7abacafd747bbb74cf7cb3de36c1e.png\", \"username\": \"admin\", \"mobile\": \"15071525233\", \"email\": \"[email]\", \"nickname\": \"管理员\n\n---\n\nTitle: qweqwe/oauth2-authorize: 手写 OAuth 2.0 授权服务\nSite: Gitee\nDate: 2021-08-05\nURL: https://gitee.com/zengqwe/oauth2-authorize?skip_mobile=true\nSnippet: 3.在IntelliJ IDEA中，可以 使用 REST Client 调用，测试接口 可用 用户列表 |username|password|mobile|email|nickname| |-|-|-|-|-| |admin|admin|15071525233|[email]|管理员| |test|test|15076549849|[email]|测试| |doudou|doudou|15076549869|[email]|王逗逗|\n\n---\n\nTitle: POST Authorize/OAuth\nSite: Venafi Trust Protection Platform Documentation Portal\nDate: 2025-07-29\nURL: https://docs.venafi.com/Docs/25.3/TopNav/Content/SDK/AuthSDK/r-SDKa-POST-AuthorizeOAuth.php\nSnippet: Example: Use the correct scope; get a bearer token Request ``` POST https://tpp.venafi.example/vedauth/authorize/oauth { \"client_id\":\"MyApp\", \"username\":\"Admin\" \"password\":\"$WebSDKPassword\", \"scope\":\"Certificate:discover,manage,delete\", \"state\":\"r9GN3vFOwjslBPsyiuB6OA==\" } ``` Response ``` HTTP/1.1 200 OK { \"access_token\": \"7F71xjzl99T2hNUwy5l8Fw==\", \"refresh_token\": \"Mxl4x5E6t0I9Ph06v69H6g==\", \"expires_in\": 7775999, \"expires\": 1639342751, \"token_type\": \"Bearer\", \"scope\": \"Certificate:delete,dis\n\nWhen you rely on a result in your answer, cite it inline as a markdown link, e.g. [title](url)."}
{"role":"assistant","content":"Проверю детали документации и форума о сроке действия токенов Intervals.icu перед внесением исправлений.","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_BVsTxGdZN5vk5XLXsyyKtTvv","function":{"name":"FetchURL","arguments":"{\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759?page=2\"}"}}]}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_BVsTxGdZN5vk5XLXsyyKtTvv","content":"The returned content is the main text extracted from the page. If you use it in your answer, cite this page as a markdown link, e.g. [title](url).\n\n## post by pmcarlos on Aug 31, 2022\n\nThanks for your response, I’ll update my app accordingly then\n\n## post by david on Sep 2, 2022\n\nIt is as app4g says. I am planning to support multiple access tokens per app soon. That was an oversight on my part.\n\n1 year later\n\n\n## post by Leonid\\_Kholkine on Sep 21, 2023\n\nComing back to this, is multi access token already supported?\n\nThanks!\n\n10 days later\n\n\n## post by david on Oct 1, 2023\n\nI just implemented that. There can be many access tokens for an athlete linked to an app, once for each time they authorise it. The most recent scopes apply to all access tokens.\n\n1 month later\n\n\n## post by Leonid\\_Kholkine on Nov 7, 2023\n\nThanks! One more question, is there also a scope for managing my athletes? The use case it’s that coaches will be connecting to intervals.\n\nEDIT: Found it in Swagger, there is a ATHLETES scope, but still doesn’t seem to work.\n\nEDIT2: It seems accessing /athletes seems to work with my own API key but not through the bearer token where I get 403.\n\n## post by david on Nov 8, 2023\n\nCurrently oauth tokens grant access to the authorising athlete’s data but not to people they follow or coach. This is by design so someone who follows you can’t auth a 3rd party app which then gains access to your data. I think you need to get each athlete to auth your app and then use the correct token depending on the athlete.\n\nWill this work?\n\n## post by Leonid\\_Kholkine on Nov 8, 2023\n\nThe only (specific) issue to us, it’s that we work with coaches and use there data. Unfortunatly our whole data platform is built around the idea of 1 connection → multiple athletes. This was following the same logic as TrainingPeaks basically, where the coached athletes are also available through the API.\n\n7 months later\n\n\n## post by Aart\\_Goossens on Jun 12, 2024\n\nIs there a way to have intervals.icu push new activities for a user to an application?\n\nAlternatively, I could regularly poll the API for new activities. Is there a rate limit in place that would limit this solution?\n\nThe rate limiting question is also relevant for the backfill scenario (where users first authorize the application and where the applications needs to process historical activities). Are there any limitations on doing that?\n\n## post by david on Jun 13, 2024\n\n\nThere are are rate limits but they are very generous and you aren’t likely to get a 429. They are there mostly to protect the server app from bugs in the Intervals.icu client\n\n![image1](https://kimi-web-img.kimi.ai/prod-data/online-image/search-upload/39a7d733bfd9e00ee3fd31c2b41c7238.png)\n\nSo backfill shouldn’t be a problem.\n\nThere is some undocumented support for webhooks. If you send me one or two web hook URLs (e.g. one dev one prod). I will set that up for you.\n\n## post by Aart\\_Goossens on Jun 13, 2024\n\nThanks for the reply. I’ll reach out to you as soon as I’m ready for integration!\n\n6 months later\n\n\n## post by david on Dec 6, 2024\n\nThere is now a management page for each OAuth application. You can view your client\\_id and secret, change redirect URL’s, enable webhooks and so on. Apps that you own on the /settings page get a “Manage App” button:\n\n\n![image2](https://kimi-web-img.kimi.ai/prod-data/online-image/search-upload/ef7703e10049bf07ae1b507e4796aacc.png)\n\n![image3](https://kimi-web-img.kimi.ai/prod-data/online-image/search-upload/f5938d5f8d27d450a374fc2a82cec171.png)\n\n2 months later\n\n\n## post by John\\_Peters\\_endura.f on Feb 4, 2025\n\nHi David - just noticed this. Does this mean you have webhooks in intervals now as well as the REST API?\n\nCheers\n\nJohn\n\n## post by david on Feb 4, 2025\n\nYes that is correct. You can just tick the boxes for the ones you want to receive.\n\n## post by John\\_Peters\\_endura.f on Feb 4, 2025\n\nJust trying to test this using the wellness updated endpoint. Is it a POST method required at my end to receive the data? I don’t seem to be getting anything coming through at the moment when I change my wellness data\n\n## post by david on Feb 4, 2025\n\nYes it is a POST. I forgot to mention that in the doc and have just added it.\n\n## post by John\\_Peters\\_endura.f on Feb 4, 2025\n\nThanks. Is there an easy way of figuring out what I’m doing wrong. My endpoints work testing in postman when I send a json file (I’m just dumping it in a DB for the moment), but I’m not getting anything through from Intervals when I change my calendar or wellness data.\n\n## post by david on Feb 4, 2025\n\nIts giving a 404:\n\n> 2025-02-04 14:12:29.248 DEBUG 1 — \\[ok-publisher-12\\] i.i.service.WebhookPublisherService : Error posting webhook i68403:WELLNESS\\_UPDATED:2025-02-04 xxx/, retry(4): icu.intervals.util.HttpStatusCodeException: Got 404 {“error”:“404 - Resource Not Found”}\n\nThat xxx is your webhook URL. Realised I shouldn’t post that here!\n\n3 months later\n\n\n## post by Aart\\_Goossens on Apr 25, 2025\n\nIt looks like wildcard redirect uris for applications are not working properly and result in an “Invalid redirect\\_uri” error. The hint for “ http://localhost/\\*” on the application management page suggests that wildcard redirect uris are supported.\n\nIn my case, “ https://app.sweatstack.no/\\*” didn’t work, but providing the full redirect uri did.\n\nAlthough some (most?) cases can be handled with the `state` query parameter, it would be nice to support wildcard redirect uris.\n\n## post by david on Apr 28, 2025\n\nI see. Yes wildcards are not supported. I will see what I can do about that.\n\n14 days later\n\n\n## post by Lady\\_Jesikat on May 13, 2025\n\nAlso, for localhost URIs, can the port number be ignored?"}
{"role":"assistant","content":"Форум не упоминает ни истечения токенов, ни refresh-токенов — это подтверждает вывод из документации: у Intervals.icu токен живёт до отзыва. Картина полная, три причины ясны. Вношу исправления.\n\n**Причина 1 — кнопка 401:** в `app.js:28` Connect — обычная `<a href>`, браузерная навигация не несёт `Authorization: Bearer` (его добавляет только fetch-обёртка), сервер отвечает 401.\n\n**Причина 2 — 400 invalid_request:** в `SCOPES` на каждую категорию запрошены оба модификатора (`ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE`, `CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`). Документация Intervals.icu: «for each scope specify READ or WRITE (to update, implies READ access)» — один модификатор на категорию. Подтверждение в логах: грантовый ответ за 2026-09-19 — ровно по одному на категорию (`ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ`), а 400 начался после релиза календарного синка, переписавшего SCOPES.\n\n**Причина 3 — почасовое «expired, reconnect»:** Intervals.icu не возвращает ни `expires_in`, ни `refresh_token` (пример ответа в документации и в логе от 2026-09-19 идентичны), механизма обновления нет. Код сам ставил TTL 3600 с и «обновлятель» переводил связь в expired — так Rivera потеряла связь через час.\n\nНачинаю с конфига и сервера:","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_cw5xRhZsFMmRiE4J3IKUsdoO","function":{"name":"Edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"config.py\",\"old_string\":\"SCOPES = \\\"ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\\\"\\n\\nREFRESH_INTERVAL = 60      # seconds between passes of the token refresher\",\"new_string\":\"# One modifier per scope category (Intervals.icu: \\\"for each scope specify READ or\\n# WRITE (to update, implies READ access)\\\"). WRITE implies READ, so this covers\\n# reading activities/wellness and writing planned workouts to the calendar.\\nSCOPES = \\\"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\\\"\"}"}}]}
